            "paragraph": "In contrast to the rapid warming in the Arctic, severely cold winters have occurred more frequently at midlatitudes. Although the exact cause is still being debated (e.g., Barnes and Screen, 2015), Mori et al. (2014) have shown, using en- semble experiments with an atmospheric general circulation model, that the more frequent cold winters at midlatitudes can be partly explained by the sea ice decrease in the Barents and Kara Seas.",
